Can you run a Windows container on Docker installed on Linux?
 The short answer: No. And here's why👇
Containers share the host OS kernel, which means:
🐧 Linux Docker = only runs Linux containers
🪟 Windows Docker = only runs Windows containers
Since Windows containers require the Windows kernel, they simply won’t run on a Linux-based Docker engine.
🛠️ Workarounds?
Spin up a Windows VM and run Docker there.
Use cloud providers like Azure or AWS that offer Windows container support.
💡 Lesson: When working with containers, understanding the host kernel and compatibility is key. Docker isn’t magic—it’s smart OS-level virtualization.
